# base_unittests tests that do not pass on Jam OS yet (tools/cr-test.sh base,
# tools/cr/base-run.py): one line each, "<pattern> <layer> <reason>". The
# pattern is a test's full name with * as the wildcard. The tests are not
# run (CR_BASE_ALL=1 runs them anyway and reports a failure as known), so a
# `base` PASS means every other test passed.
#
# SEEDED FROM ONE SHARD ONLY. The first run (2026-10-15, shard 0 of 4 of the
# suites, 144 suites, 1885 tests) is all that has been triaged: the other
# shards hung or never started (the test PC's queue stopped answering), so
# this list is a start, not the whole list, and a full `base` run will name
# more. The layer is the track that owns the fix (docs/CR-PLAN.md); "?" in
# the reason marks a cause that is a guess from the failing call, not seen.

# ---- crashes with no output: SIGABRT about 0.8 s after the program starts
# (gtest's death-test machinery or a test that expects to die; no ENOSYS
# line was logged for them, so the missing call is not known).
*DeathTest.*                      posix  SIGABRT at the start of the death test; cause not seen (fork or clone for the death test child?)
ClampTest.Death                   posix  same
FlatMap.AtFunction                posix  same (a CHECK death test)
OptionalTest.DereferencingNoValueCrashes posix same
Debugger.CrashAtBreakpoint        posix  same
MultiMemoryConsumerTest.DuplicateInterventionsCheck posix same
PersistentMemoryAllocatorTest.DelayedAllocationTest posix same
HistogramSnapshotManagerTest.PrepareDeltasUmaStabilityHistogramFlagFilter posix same (a death test; the program ends with code 0)

# ---- /data is FAT: no symlinks, no named pipes, no permission bits.
FileUtilTest.*Symlink*            fs     symlink() fails on /data (errno not captured; FAT holds no symlinks?)
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryWithNonRegularFiles fs symlink() and mkfifo() fail on /data
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryExclFileOverFifo fs mkfifo() returns -1 on /data
FileUtilTest.ReadFileToStringWithNamedPipe fs mkfifo() returns -1 on /data
FileUtilTest.ChangeFilePermissions* fs   chmod has no effect: the file stays readable and writable
FileUtilTest.ChangeDirectoryPermissionsAndEnumerate fs same
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryPermissions* fs the mode stays 0644 / 0755 whatever is set
FileUtilTest.CopyFileExecutablePermission fs same
FileUtilTest.CopyFileACL          fs     the read-only mode bit is not kept
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryACL     fs     same
FileUtilTest.ExecutableExistsInPath fs   a file made executable is not found executable (mode bits?)
FileUtilTest.TouchFile            posix  utimensat does not set the times: the file keeps its own
FileProxyTest.SetTimes            posix  same
FileUtilTest.DeleteDeep           fs     mkdirat fails with "Filename too long" (which limit: a name or a path?)

# ---- calls and /proc paths the ENOSYS log named.
FileUtilTest.CopyFileContentsWithSendfile* posix sendfile (syscall 40) is ENOSYS
FileUtilTest.ReadFileToStringWithProcFileSystem proc /proc/cpuinfo is not there
FileUtilTest.CopyFileContentsWithSendfileSeqFile proc /proc/meminfo is not there

# ---- a writable shared mapping of a file on /data.
MemoryMappedFileTest.WriteableFile fs    MemoryMappedFile READ_WRITE initialisation fails (mmap MAP_SHARED PROT_WRITE of a /data file?)
MemoryMappedFileTest.ExtendableFile fs   same
PersistentMemoryAllocatorTest.TruncateTest fs same

# ---- starting other programs: base::LaunchProcess / fork. Plan: the
# launcher patch of CB5 (docs/CR-PLAN.md section 5); until then these fail.
ProcessUtilTest.*                 launch process.IsValid() is false after SpawnMultiProcessTestChild / LaunchProcess (no fork line in the log: which call fails is not known)
ForkWithFlagsTest.*               posix  fork returns -1 (syscall 57 is ENOSYS)
LoggingTest.AlwaysLogErrorsToStderr posix fork (syscall 57) is ENOSYS
LoggingTest.CheckCausesDistinctBreakpoints posix fork returns -1
ProcessGTestOutputTest.*          launch the test launcher's mock-test children cannot start (fork, syscall 57)
